<title>FRANCE: Right's lead slightly cut in French election poll.</title>
<headline>Right's lead slightly cut in French election poll.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an opinion poll of voters' intentions ahead of the May 25/June 1 parliamentary election.</p>
<p>The telephone poll of 1,005 adults aged 18 and over was conducted by Louis Harris on May 15 and 16 for LCI television and made public on Saturday.</p>
<p>			   percentage  projected seats in</p>
<p>			    of vote    National Assembly</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		2		-</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		  9.5	    -</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Socialists-other left  27		-</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Ecologists		  7		-</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> RPR/UDF-other right    39		-</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> National Front	   15		-</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------</p>
